myList = {10, 20, 15, 30}
Running = List.Accumulate(myList, {}, (state, current) => state & {List.Sum(state) + current})
List.Accumulate starts with seed {} and builds up. Each step adds the cumulative sum to the result list. For simple total: List.Accumulate(myList, 0, (state, current) => state + current) — simpler than List.Sum for understanding the pattern.
